display the target's definition location, hover docs, and signature

Usage:
  gopls [flags] inspect [inspect-flags] <target>

Example:
	$ gopls inspect -pkg go/ast Decl
	$ gopls inspect golang.org/x/tools/go/ast/inspector.Cursor

inspect-flags:
  -full
    	returns the entire doc comment for the entity, otherwise just the synopsis is returned
  -json
    	emit output in JSON format
  -markdown
    	outputs documentation in formatted Markdown instead of plain text
  -pkg=string
    	scopes the query to a specific package, resolving ambiguities in versioned package paths (for example, gopkg.in/yaml.v3) or vanity domains.
  -pos=location
    	targets a file span. Format: file.go[:lineStart[:colStart]-lineEnd[:colEnd]], file.go[:line:colStart-colEnd], or file.go[:#offsetStart-#offsetEnd] (1-based line, 1-based column in UTF-8 bytes, 0-based byte offset). Also accepts a single point, returning a location that has that point as both the start and end.
  -src
    	prints the source code of the definition (declaration and body)
